Function build_recommend_full_build_benchmark_cases:
- define exactly 5 `recommend_full_build` benchmark scenarios
- keep hero selections distinct across cases
- intentionally vary owned item counts from 0 through 4 so the benchmark covers early, mid, and late build-completion states


Function load_model_refs_from_env_file:
- read `.env` directly for `ALL_MODEL` first and `ALL_MODELS` second
- fall back to already-loaded settings only when the file parse does not provide a model matrix
- reuse the shared eval model parser so provider/model validation stays consistent


Function filter_model_refs:
- optionally narrow the loaded model list to one or more provider names and/or model identifiers
- accept repeated CLI-style values or comma-separated provider/model lists
- match provider names, bare model names, full `provider/model` labels, and `.env`-style `provider:model` strings case-insensitively
- raise a clear error when filtering removes every model


Function sync_model_price_table:
- treat the configured JSON file as a persistent model-price registry rather than a per-run overwrite
- keep the default registry under `scripts/recommend_full_build_model_prices.json` so it lives with benchmark tooling rather than generated reports
- preserve every previously saved model entry so filtered benchmark runs cannot delete older prices
- refresh provider/model identity fields for the models included in the current run while keeping their saved prices and notes
- add blank entries for brand-new models so the user can fill them later


Function build_selected_model_price_table:
- derive a benchmark-local price snapshot from the persistent registry
- keep only the models selected for the current run while preserving their saved prices and notes
- reuse the registry timestamp when available so per-run artifacts can point back to the synced registry state


Function build_default_output_dir:
- create a timestamped output directory path under `evaluation_reports/` for one recommend_full_build benchmark run


Function run_recommend_full_build_benchmark:
- build the 5 benchmark cases
- sync the persistent model-price registry on disk
- derive a current-run-only price snapshot from that registry
- run every case against every requested model with provider/model overrides
- show a `tqdm` progress bar during manual benchmark runs while allowing tests to disable it
- optionally print one-line failure summaries to the terminal as soon as a case fails
- collect per-run outputs, timing, token usage, and cost metadata
- write JSON, Markdown, case snapshot, and current-run model-price snapshot artifacts


Function render_recommend_full_build_benchmark_markdown:
- render a compact manual-review-friendly report covering model-level summary stats plus per-case generated content and explanation text
- when a case fails, include a concise failure summary plus error code, status, parsed issue list, and raw error details in the Markdown report


Function _run_one_case:
- execute one non-stream `recommend_full_build` run with cache disabled
- measure total wall-clock elapsed time around the full backend pipeline
- capture run-level latency, token counters, provider-reported cost, estimated cost from the user-editable price table, generated build content, and explanation text
- return a failure record with the error string plus structured failure metadata when execution raises


Function _summarize_results:
- aggregate benchmark rows by model and compute average elapsed time, average tokens, and total cost fields


Function _write_benchmark_artifacts:
- persist the benchmark report as JSON and Markdown
- persist the resolved case list and the price-table snapshot alongside the report


Function _extract_generated_content:
- pull the build order, rune recommendation, and slot notes out of the raw recommend_full_build result for easier comparison


Function _estimate_cost_from_price_table:
- compute USD cost from input/output tokens only when both token counts and both per-million prices are available


Function _build_failure_error_payload:
- normalize an exception plus any persisted run error fields into one benchmark-friendly failure payload
- preserve a concise failure summary, error code, HTTP status, parsed detail payload, and human-readable issue lines when available


Function _read_model_matrix_from_env_file:
- parse a simple `.env` file line by line
- support both `ALL_MODEL` and `ALL_MODELS`
- return the comma-split provider:model entries


Function _normalize_filter_values:
- flatten repeated CLI filter arguments and comma-separated values into one normalized lowercase set


Function _model_filter_candidates:
- generate the accepted identifier variants for one model ref
- include bare model name, `provider/model`, and `.env`-style `provider:model`


Function _extract_error_issue_messages:
- convert structured validation issues from an error details payload into readable `path: message` lines


Function _json_safe_error_details:
- keep error details JSON-serializable for report.json and report.md output


Function _build_model_price_table_payload:
- standardize the JSON payload shape used by both the persistent registry file and per-run model-price snapshots
- sort model labels for stable diffs and easier manual editing
- stamp the payload with either the provided sync time or the current UTC time


Function _read_json_file:
- load a JSON object from disk and safely return an empty dict on missing/invalid content


Function _strip_wrapping_quotes:
- remove one matching pair of outer single or double quotes from an env value


Function _owned_item_count:
- count how many build slots are already populated in the benchmark case context


Function _avg:
- compute a rounded mean across numeric values only


Function _sum:
- compute a rounded numeric sum across numeric values only


Function _display_number:
- render optional numeric report fields in Markdown tables


Function _display_currency:
- render optional USD values with fixed precision for Markdown tables


Function _context:
- build a valid `MatchContext` from simplified benchmark inputs


Function _slots:
- enforce the correct slot count for LoL vs Wild Rift benchmark cases


Function _runes:
- package the primary/secondary rune lists into the expected payload shape
